<title>MEXICO: Penoles plans to hike metal content output.</title>
<headline>Penoles plans to hike metal content output.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Industrias Penoles, the world's largest refined silver producer, outlined plans to increase output of metal content in the period 1996-2000.</p>
<p>Below is a table of the changes planned in its mining division, figures in percentages. The 2000 goal includes three future mines. No other details were given.</p>
<p>  Metal			   1996		     2000</p>
<p>  Gold			     19			199</p>
<p>  Silver			   23			 30</p>
<p>  Lead				2			 25</p>
<p>  Zinc			     14			 93</p>
<p>Penoles said the above outlook table does not include or consider potential acquisitions, development of new businesses nor prospects under exploration.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287902))</p>
